    Check the stage lists against the sized stages and the runs
    
    The trusted planner now checks two relations between the solved stages and a
    run: a planned list longer than the stage's sized random coordinates is
    rejected with its stage, and the run's stage sizes must match the solved ones
    in the stage count, the fold bits, the main and mask lengths and the code
    lengths, each mismatch naming the stage and the field. Unit tests cover both
    checks and their named failures.
    
    This is the structural part of the whole-chain budget check; the per-round
    round counts and the total budget remain the next step.

